From 07bfdb1e4a3827a1335f95f727ca0d2752c02279 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dispatch Sandbox <jax1313@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:00:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] Repair the operational proof path and make it
 executable

Steps 18, 19 and 20 are the only Code-automated steps in PROOF_PATH -- the
gate between IMPLEMENTED and OPERATIONALLY PROVEN -- and all three invoked
commands the programs reject:

  18  dispatch_proof.py verify --load-id      invalid choice: 'verify'
  19  dispatch_backup.py create --destination invalid choice: 'create'
  20  dispatch_backup.py restore --archive .. unrecognized arguments

They are tuple literals, so coverage saw them run and nothing executed them.

Step 18's subcommand never existed, so it is built rather than deleted: the
step's own note describes real work ("compares record identifiers and evidence
SHA-256 hashes against step 12/14") and dispatch/proof.py already had the
comparison helpers. verify_persistence() recomputes each evidence file's hash
off disk against the checksum attach_evidence() recorded at upload, so it needs
no prior snapshot -- the database is the snapshot -- and snapshot/--snapshot add
the stricter before-and-after comparison that also catches records which
appeared from nowhere.

Steps 19 and 20 are corrected to the real CLI. restore already recomputes every
hash before writing anything, so there is no --verify flag to pass and never was.

tests/test_proof_command_contract.py parses every `python scripts/...` command
in PROOF_PATH through that tool's own build_parser(). Verified to fail on each
of the three original strings.
